From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Erik Bourget <erik@ebourget.net>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 12:08:27 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] dt-bindings: display: apple,dcp: note the T8132 dcpext
 bandwidth slot

The T8132 external DCPs take apple,bw-scratch for their 8-byte realtime
bandwidth request slot in the PMC. Unlike the other DCPs, where the
scratch register becomes an extra display register window, the slot lies
inside the window the display index names (disp-4). Say so in the
property's description.

Signed-off-by: Erik Bourget <erik@ebourget.net>
(cherry picked from commit 0a64760421a6131276cc85d511850da044fd2dbc)
---
 Documentation/devicetree/bindings/display/apple,dcp.yaml | 5 ++++-
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/display/apple,dcp.yaml b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/display/apple,dcp.yaml
index b4cbe622ca..66e341e7e9 100644
--- a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/display/apple,dcp.yaml
+++ b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/display/apple,dcp.yaml
@@ -117,7 +117,10 @@ properties:
           - description: Index into the provider's reg property.
           - description: Index in the firmware display register table.
           - description: Byte offset of the scratch register within the resource.
-    description: PMGR bandwidth scratch resource, display index and offset.
+    description: |
+      PMGR bandwidth scratch resource, display index and offset. On the T8132
+      external DCPs it is the pipe's 8-byte realtime bandwidth request slot,
+      which lies inside the display register window the index names (disp-4).
 
   apple,bw-doorbell:
     $ref: /schemas/types.yaml#/definitions/phandle-array
